            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Trevesia palmata is a small tree up to {{cvt|6|m}} height. It is in the family Araliaceae, and is native to Southeast Asia, from India to southern China. The common name is snowflake tree The leaves can be very unusual, sometimes with a central leaflet to which as many as nine peripheral leaflets are attached. These leaflets may be lobed to various degrees, each attached to the central leaflet by a petiolule."
          }
        ]
